Grayswindr is probably the best weapon in the game and a
tourist can become skilled so that's the top end game weapon
for a tourist. If you're not lawful, getting GS may be a
problem even a premature wish might kill you. Next best is
probably Frost Brand even though the tourist can only become
basic. 

Other artifact long swords that you would want if you can't
get either GS or Frost Brand are Demonbane, Excalibur,
Snickersnee, Vorpral Blade, Fire Brand and Sunsword.
Grimtooth and Magicbane use the dagger skill and should take
you far into the game.

So, mid game, any long sword, katana or saber you can get
your hands on before you get one of the artifacts mentioned
above.

Early, the tourist can become expert with daggers and darts.
I would go for daggers since they don't get used up. Two
weaponing carries some pretty serious "to hit" penalties so,
if you use it in the early game, practice on things that
aren't very dangerous. Rocks are free and effective for
killing things that would mess up your daggers. I wouldn't
routinely carry them but I often go get a pile for sea
creatures or a P.

Now if you spent 6 slots each on daggers and two weaponing,
5 on darts, 3 on saber and one on long sword you would need
21 skill slots which you can earn at XL22. If I wanted to
economize, I wouldn't advance darts or two weaponing to
expert saving 6 skill slots for spellcasting skills. I would
advance daggers to expert since I need the "to hit" and
damage bonuses early in the game when I'll depend on my
daggers the most.

Most like a silver second weapon so they are prepared when
the silver haters, particularly the shades, come along. But
if you can't get GS, go with a silver dagger at expert and
don't develop saber at all.

